-#   - port 15021 (/healthz/ready): no application pod needs the probe port, so it
-#     stays unlisted. NOTE: Cilium currently runs with `enable-host-firewall=false`,
-#     which is an observation about today's config, NOT a guarantee that a kubelet
-#     probe and its reply are unaffected by pod-level policy. The Firecrawl egress
-#     incident (docs/troubleshooting/mcp-firecrawl-egress-regression.md) is a
-#     precedent where egress-only policies were associated with kubelet probe
-#     timeouts, but the mechanism was never established. So nothing here assumes
-#     replies are exempt, and no blanket host / remote-node allow is added.
-#     IMPORTANT: networkIsolation is currently false (owner authorized policy-free
-#     baseline first). Do not enable until this legacy K8s NetworkPolicy is replaced
-#     with a reviewed CiliumNetworkPolicy that properly handles node-sourced probes.
-#   - the agentgateway admin address: bound to "off" in the config, so there is
-#     nothing to reach.
-#   - NodePort / loadBalancer / hostPort: the Service is ClusterIP only.
